-- title:
--   Chains closed modulo Γ have periods in the period lattice
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma$ be a finite-index subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, and let $Z$ be a finitely supported function from $\mathfrak{H}\times\mathfrak{H}$ to $\mathbb{Z}$, regarded as an integral $1$-chain whose generators are the ordered pairs $e=(e_1,e_2)$ of points of the upper half-plane with multiplicity $m=Z(e)$. Assume that the boundary of $Z$ vanishes modulo $\Gamma$, in the sense that for every $\tau\in\mathfrak{H}$ the sum over the support of $Z$ of $m$ taken over those $e$ with $e_2$ in the orbit $\Gamma\tau$, minus the sum of $m$ over those $e$ with $e_1$ in the orbit $\Gamma\tau$, is $0$. Then the functional $\sum_e m\cdot\mathrm{periodAlongOf}\,\Gamma\,e_1\,e_2$ lies in $\mathrm{periodLatticeOf}\,\Gamma$. Here $\mathrm{periodAlongOf}\,\Gamma\,\tau_0\,\tau_1$ is the element of the $\mathbb{C}$-linear dual of $\mathrm{CuspForm}(\Gamma,2)$ sending $f$ to $\int_0^1 f(\mathrm{segmentPath}\,\tau_0\,\tau_1\,t)\,(\tau_1-\tau_0)\,dt$, and $\mathrm{periodLatticeOf}\,\Gamma$ is the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of that dual spanned by the functionals $\mathrm{periodOf}\,\Gamma\,\gamma=\mathrm{periodAlongOf}\,\Gamma\,i\,(\gamma\cdot i)$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma$.
--
--   This is the Abel-type statement that a $1$-chain of geodesic-free straight segments in $\mathfrak{H}$ which becomes a cycle on $\Gamma\backslash\mathfrak{H}$ has period functional in the lattice generated by the periods $f\mapsto\int_i^{\gamma i}f$, $\gamma\in\Gamma$; the proof uses only the existence of a $\Gamma$-equivariant primitive of a weight-$2$ cusp form, via [`ModularCurve.exists_hasEquivariantPrimitiveOf`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_hasEquivariantPrimitiveOf). It is used in the study of period lattices of modular curves at arbitrary finite level, notably by [`ModularCurve.periodAlongOf_add_petersson_mem_periodLatticeOf_of_multiplier_eq_exp`](thm.html#ModularCurve.periodAlongOf_add_petersson_mem_periodLatticeOf_of_multiplier_eq_exp).
